# Project Governance

## Source of truth

- **`docs/project/`** and **`docs/tasks/`** come first. Chat is not trusted.
- If docs and chat disagree, **fix the docs first**, then implement.
- The human operations board (Notion) syncs only **summary, status, priority, branch, docs path, and result summary**. Detailed body content lives only in `docs/tasks/*.md`.

## One TASK at a time

- Implementation must belong to **a single TASK**.
- Do not work outside the TASK **Scope / Acceptance Criteria**.
- Use the TASK ID (`TASK-NNN`) consistently in every commit message, branch name, and log entry.

## Protect the MVP scope

- Do **not add** features that are not listed in `docs/project/02-mvp-scope.md`.
- Convenience items such as hosting, realtime sync, webhooks, and automatic LLM calls are introduced only through separate TASKs.

## Refactors and integrations

- Large refactors are allowed only when covered by **a separate TASK**.
- External integrations (Git host API, Notion, messengers, and similar systems) are allowed **only when the TASK explicitly says so**.
